# ── OS / editor cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.asv
*.m~

# ── MATLAB generated ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.mex*
slprj/
codegen/

# ── Data, cache and exports (never committed) ────────────────────────
# These live outside version control; see dependencies.md.
Data/
*.mat
*.csv
*.erp
*.i
*.Rhistory
*.BLE
ga.txt

# ── Vendored toolkits (kept locally, obtained externally) ────────────
# The app expects these on the MATLAB path at runtime. They are NOT
# tracked here; see dependencies.md for versions and sources.
/eeglab/
/eeglab2024.2/
/eeglabolder/

# ── Stray working folders ────────────────────────────────────────────
/dummy/
+uiextras/+jTree/Tree2.m

# ── src/webtree/ (WorkSpaceTree.m's JS build tooling) ─────────────────
# The build OUTPUT is vendored at src/WorkSpaceTree.html; node_modules and
# the intermediate (pre-inlining) bundle are not committed. See
# src/webtree/README.md to rebuild.
src/webtree/node_modules/
src/webtree/dist/

# ── src/help/ (the in-app help viewer's build tooling) ────────────────
# Nothing here is committed, INCLUDING the built page itself: it embeds
# every screenshot as base64 and runs to ~5 MB, and it is regenerated
# from readme.MD, so committing it would put a 5 MB binary-ish diff in
# history every time the readme changed. Build it with
# `npm install && npm run build` in src/help, then copy dist/
# AlakazamHelp.html up to src/ (see src/help/README.md). Alakazam.onHelp
# explains what to do if it is missing rather than failing.
src/help/node_modules/
src/help/dist/
src/AlakazamHelp.html
